\begin{definition}[Volume~I Grounding Contract: Homotopy-Fiber Defect and Categorical Residuum]\label{vol1:def:residuum}%
Pinned read-only to Volume~I (\texttt{def:residuum}, \texttt{docs/categorical\_reverse\_mathematics.tex:643}, Zenodo DOI \texttt{10.5281/zenodo.24238086})~\cite{Shulman20,Johnstone02}. Evaluated at $X \in \mathcal{D}_0$, a comparison functor $F_X : \mathcal{A}(X) \to \mathcal{B}(X)$ induces the \textbf{mode-$n$ core homotopy-fiber defect} ($n \in \{-1, 0, \infty\}$) $\|\mathrm{hofib}_y(F_X^{\simeq})\|_n := \|\mathcal{A}(X)^{\simeq} \times^h_{\mathcal{B}(X)^{\simeq}} \{y\}\|_n$ and the \textbf{mapping-anima homotopy-fiber defect} $\|\mathrm{hofib}_g(F_{X; a,a'})\|_n$. A \textbf{categorical residuum} $\mathcal{R} = \mathrm{Res}(\kappa)$ is an admissible invariant on $\mathcal{D}_0$ characterizing the vanishing locus $\mathcal{D}_1$ via the Fundamental Equivalence $\mathcal{D}_0 + \mathrm{Res}(\kappa) \iff \mathcal{D}_1$.
\end{definition}

